185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In Azure Data Factory \(ADF\), schema drift is handled using Mapping Data Flows with the Allow Schema Drift option enabled. This allows dynamic handling of changes in the schema \(e.g., added or removed columns\) without manual intervention. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The Source transformation detects schema changes, and the Auto Mapping feature in Sink maps columns automatically.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (You can also use the Select transformation to explicitly choose or remove columns dynamically. This makes the data flow adaptable to evolving schemas across different sources.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
